CommitDate: Sat Jan 14 11:14:44 2017 +0100

    locking/ww_mutex: Optimize ww-mutexes by waking at most one waiter for =
backoff when acquiring the lock
    =

    The wait list is sorted by stamp order, and the only waiting task that =
may
    have to back off is the first waiter with a context.
    =

    The regular slow path does not have to wake any other tasks at all, sin=
ce
    all other waiters that would have to back off were either woken up when
    the waiter was added to the list, or detected the condition before they
    added themselves.
    =

    Median timings taken of a contention-heavy GPU workload:
    =

    Without this series:
    =

      real    0m59.900s
      user    0m7.516s
      sys     2m16.076s
    =

    With changes up to and including this patch:
    =

      real    0m52.946s
      user    0m7.272s
      sys     1m55.964s
    =

